        t = 1 for c in [0.04045, 1]\n          by monotonicity in c (each a preimage of a value class):\n            b = +inf, b*0 = NaN: never\n            b = -inf, b*0 = NaN: never\n            a = -0 and b*0 = +0: for c = -0 (original +0, select -0)\n            a = +inf, a*0 = NaN: never\n            a = -inf, a*0 = NaN: never\n            b = -0 and a*0 = +0: never\n          every difference is in the sign of a zero or an infinity against a NaN: within Vulkan's default float controls (no SignedZeroInfNanPreserve): the sign of a zero, infinities and NaNs need not be preserved\n        not bit-exact at c = -0 (original +0, select -0)\n        (line 1: vec3 decode(vec3 c) { return mix(c / 12.92, pow((c + 0.055) / 1.055, vec3(2.4)), step(vec3)\n    %61 = OpExtInst %v3float %2 Pow %60 %26\n      -> %ucas_f2l = OpExtInst %v3float %2 Log2 %60\n         %ucas_f2m = OpFMul %v3float %ucas_f2l %26\n         %61 = OpExtInst %v3float %2 Exp2 %ucas_f2m\n      (pow as exp2(y * log2 x); -3)\n      proof: within the original's Vulkan precision (derived), not bit-exact\n        where it is used, the base (c + 0.055) * 0.94786733 is in [0.090473935, 1] (only the select's side for it)\n          Vulkan: pow: inherited from exp2(y * log2(x)); exp2: 3 + 2|x| ulp; log2: 3 ulp outside [0.5, 2], absolute error < 2^-21 inside; the rewrite is that expression, so its bound is the original's by definition: within\n          against the correctly rounded pow: L = log2(q)(1 + d1), t = y L (1 + d2), |t^ - t| <= |t|(2u + u^2) with |t| <= 8.319 here, so exp2(t^)(1 + d3) = q^y 2^(t^ - t)(1 + d3): relative error < 7.47e-07, under 13.5 ulp of a result within 0.5 ulp\n          considered, none cheaper than exp2(y * log2 x) at 9:\n            x^2.4 as x*x*pow(x, 0.4): a pow remains (10 + 2)\n            x^2.4 by 3 sqrt and 3 multiplies (exponent 2.375): 27, and an approximation: q^(0.0250001) - 1 reaches 0.0583 on the base's range\n            the integer seed asfloat(int(2.4 * (asuint(q) - 0x3f8